    "coulomb-encounter-offaxis": {
      "supplementary_chapter": "chapters/10-collisions-conductivity.html",
      "supplementary_description": "Two electrons approach with impact parameter b = 2 reduced de Broglie wavelengths at Sommerfeld parameter eta = 3, the same encounter as the head-on case in Chapter 10 but off axis. Four panels on one logarithmic colour scale show the probability density of the relative coordinate in the plane of the encounter: a classical Wigner-sampled ensemble, the distinguishable (spin-unresolved) quantum packet, and the singlet and triplet states. The classical and distinguishable panels keep the region inside the head-on turning radius r0 = 2 eta reduced wavelengths nearly empty, and the outgoing density is tilted rather than symmetric about the collision axis; singlet and triplet add exchange fringes of opposite sign, and their average is the distinguishable panel. Positions k x and k z, with k the inverse reduced wavelength, and the time t v/z0 are normalized, with unit [1]. Data: kin6d partial-wave propagation; a visualization without pointwise error bounds.",
