      "supplementary_chapter": "chapters/05-single-particle-motion.html",
      "supplementary_description": "Full Lorentz-force orbits of an ion and an electron in a magnetic field B = B0(1 + y/L) along z that grows in y, with L = 10 ion Larmor radii, reduced mass ratio 16 and equal temperatures. The orbit is tighter where B is stronger, so the guiding centres drift along x in opposite directions for the two charges. The measured drift speeds agree with mu grad B x B/(q B^2) within 1.3 % (ion) and 0.1 % (electron). Lengths in ion Larmor radii and time in inverse ion gyrofrequencies, with unit [1]."
    },
