      "supplementary_chapter": "chapters/05-single-particle-motion.html",
      "supplementary_description": "Full Lorentz-force orbits of an ion and an electron in the toroidal vacuum field B proportional to 1/R, shown in the poloidal plane. The combined curvature and grad-B drift moves the ion up and the electron down, a charge separation that a purely toroidal field cannot hold. The measured vertical drift speeds agree with (m/(q B R))(v_par^2 + v_perp^2/2) within 1.6 % (ion) and 0.4 % (electron). Lengths in ion Larmor radii, with unit [1]."
